IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively): section 2036a of the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2036a), "Nutrition
-- education and obesity prevention grant program", lines 3142-3263 of usc07-ch51.txt (snap6's third range).
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the OLRC's USLM XML. It is not the official text, and
-- nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- READING A RESULT: a MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE NUMBER answers JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, JUST TRUE
-- where it says yes, and NOTHING everywhere else ("not covered"). Every branch says which kind it is.
-- MONEY is a NUMBER of dollars; a percentage input is a figure in percent (10 means ten percent).
-- "The Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service" is acted for by `the Secretary` (the core has no Administrator:
-- NEEDS-CORE.md, fork FR-36a-2).

-- HELPERS (not a rule of the Act): three-valued AND / OR over MAYBE BOOLEAN, so that a NOTHING input is passed through
-- unless another limb decides the answer without it (PLAN.md section 4).
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a every one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) xs THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): one limb is the text's no, so the whole is, wherever that no came from
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb says no
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: every limb holds

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a at least one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) xs THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: one limb holds
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb holds
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): every limb is the text's no

§ `s 2036a -- Nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program`

-- TYPES this section needs (none is in the core).

-- (c)(1): how a State agency delivers services.
DECLARE `s 2036a delivery` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036a directly to eligible individuals`
    `s 2036a through agreements with other State or local agencies or community organizations`
    `s 2036a in some other way`

-- (c)(2)(B)(iii)(II): the categories of allowable State agency administrative costs the text lists.
DECLARE `s 2036a cost category` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036a salaries and benefits of State agency personnel`
    `s 2036a office supplies and equipment`
    `s 2036a travel costs`
    `s 2036a development and production of nutrition education materials`
    `s 2036a memberships, subscriptions, and professional activities`
    `s 2036a lease or rental costs`
    `s 2036a maintenance and repair expenses`
    `s 2036a indirect costs`
    `s 2036a cost of using publicly-owned building space`
    `s 2036a some other cost`

-- (c)(2)(B): what a nutrition education State plan contains.
DECLARE `s 2036a what a plan contains` HAS
    `it identifies the uses of the funding for local projects`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it ensures that the interventions are appropriate for eligible individuals in low-income populations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it describes how the State agency shall use an electronic reporting system to measure and evaluate the projects and account for allowable administrative costs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it conforms to standards established by the Secretary`                                      IS A BOOLEAN

-- (c)(3)(A): the examples of allowable uses of funds the text gives.
DECLARE `s 2036a allowable use` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036a individual and group-based nutrition education, health promotion, and intervention strategies`
    `s 2036a comprehensive, multilevel interventions at multiple complementary organizational and institutional levels`
    `s 2036a community and public health approaches to improve nutrition`
    `s 2036a some other use`

-- (c)(3)(B): the groups the Administrator consults.
DECLARE `s 2036a stakeholder` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036a the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention`
    `s 2036a the Director of the National Institute of Food and Agriculture`
    `s 2036a representatives of the academic and research communities`
    `s 2036a nutrition education practitioners`
    `s 2036a representatives of State and local governments`
    `s 2036a community organizations that serve low-income populations`
    `s 2036a some other person or body`

-- (c)(7): the forms of technical assistance the text lists.
DECLARE `s 2036a technical assistance` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036a identifying common challenges faced by participating entities`
    `s 2036a coordinating efforts to address those common challenges`
    `s 2036a collecting and disseminating information on evidence-based practices`
    `s 2036a facilitating communication among grantees and subgrantees`
    `s 2036a assisting State agencies in creating or maintaining systems to compile program data`
    `s 2036a other activities, as determined by the Secretary`
    `s 2036a some other help`

-- (c)(8): what a State agency's annual report includes.
DECLARE `s 2036a state report` HAS
    `the use of funds, including for each category of allowable administrative costs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a description of each project, with its target population, interventions, educational materials, key performance indicators and evaluations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a comprehensive analysis of impacts and outcomes of the project and, to the extent practicable, of completed multiyear projects` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the status of any ongoing multiyear project` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (c)(9): what the annual Federal report evaluates and includes.
DECLARE `s 2036a federal report` HAS
    `it evaluates coordination with the expanded food and nutrition education program` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it evaluates coordination with any other nutrition education program administered by the Department of Agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it evaluates coordination of the nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it includes the use of funds on such programs, including State agency administrative costs reported under paragraph (8)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (d)(2)(B)(ii): how funds came to a State agency.
DECLARE `s 2036a how funds came to the State agency` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036a received through a reallocation`
    `s 2036a surrendered by the State agency`
    `s 2036a some other way`

-- (d)(3)(A): where Federal financial participation comes from.
DECLARE `s 2036a source of Federal financial participation` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036a a grant awarded under this section`
    `s 2036a any other source`

-- (b), (c): the acts the State agency, the Secretary and the Administrator are told to do.
DECLARE `s 2036a act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036a implement a nutrition education and obesity prevention program`
    `s 2036a submit a nutrition education State plan to the Secretary for approval`
    `s 2036a consult the Directors and outside stakeholders and experts`
    `s 2036a notify applicants, participants and eligible individuals of the availability of services`
    `s 2036a establish an online clearinghouse`
    `s 2036a provide technical assistance to the State agency`
    `s 2036a submit the annual State report to the Secretary`
    `s 2036a submit the annual Federal report to the Committees`
    `s 2036a reserve the funds for allocation to State agencies`
    `s 2036a reallocate the unexpended funds to other States`

§§ `(a) Definition of eligible individual`

-- (a) "the term 'eligible individual' means an individual who is eligible to receive benefits under a nutrition education
-- and obesity prevention program under this section as a result of being (1) an individual eligible for benefits under (A) this
-- chapter; (B) sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42; or (C) section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42; (2) an individual who
-- resides in a community with a significant low-income population, as determined by the Secretary; or (3) such other low-income
-- individual as is determined to be eligible by the Secretary." The title 42 sections are outside the sources, so the person
-- states whether they are eligible under them; the Secretary's determinations and eligibility under this chapter are conditional inputs.
-- src:3143 | (a) Definition of eligible individual
-- src:3144 | In this section, the term “eligible individual” means an individual who is eligible to receive benefits under a nutrition education and obesity prevention program under this section as a result of being—
-- src:3145 | (1) an individual eligible for benefits under—
-- src:3146 | (A) this chapter;
-- src:3147 | (B) sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42; or
-- src:3148 | (C) section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42;
-- src:3149 | (2) an individual who resides in a community with a significant low-income population, as determined by the Secretary; or
-- src:3150 | (3) such other low-income individual as is determined to be eligible by the Secretary.
@ref s 2036a(a) Definition of eligible individual (src:3143-3150)
GIVEN `s 2014 the individual is eligible for benefits under this chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual is eligible for benefits under sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is eligible for benefits under section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that the individual resides in a community with a significant low-income population` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that the individual is another low-income individual who is eligible` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limbs (1) to (3)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "means an individual who is eligible ... as a result of being (1) ...; (2) ...; or (3)"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the term 'eligible individual' means" (a definition that says "means"; every limb false)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb that depends on this chapter's eligibility or on a determination of the Secretary's was not supplied and no other limb is true
    WHERE
        `the limbs (1) to (3)` MEANS
            `s 2036a at least one of these holds`
                (LIST `s 2014 the individual is eligible for benefits under this chapter`,
                      JUST `the individual is eligible for benefits under sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42`,
                      JUST `the individual is eligible for benefits under section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42`,
                      `the Secretary determines that the individual resides in a community with a significant low-income population`,
                      `the Secretary determines that the individual is another low-income individual who is eligible`)

§§ `(b) Programs`

-- (b) "Consistent with the terms and conditions of grants awarded under this section, State agencies may implement a nutrition
-- education and obesity prevention program for eligible individuals that promotes healthy food choices and physical activity
-- consistent with the most recent Dietary Guidelines for Americans published under section 5341 of this title."
-- src:3151 | (b) Programs
-- src:3152 | Consistent with the terms and conditions of grants awarded under this section, State agencies may implement a nutrition education and obesity prevention program for eligible individuals that promotes healthy food choices and physical activity consistent with the most recent Dietary Guidelines for Americans published under section 5341 of this title.
@ref s 2036a(b) Programs (src:3151-3152)
GIVEN `the individual is an eligible individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the program promotes healthy food choices and physical activity consistent with the most recent Dietary Guidelines for Americans` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the program is consistent with the terms and conditions of the grant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(b) the State agency may implement the program for the individual` MEANS
    IF `the individual is an eligible individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the program promotes healthy food choices and physical activity consistent with the most recent Dietary Guidelines for Americans`
       AND `the program is consistent with the terms and conditions of the grant`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "State agencies may implement a nutrition education and obesity prevention program for eligible individuals that promotes healthy food choices"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is for eligible individuals and a program of that kind

-- src:3151 | (b) Programs
-- src:3152 | Consistent with the terms and conditions of grants awarded under this section, State agencies may implement a nutrition education and obesity prevention program for eligible individuals that promotes healthy food choices and physical activity consistent with the most recent Dietary Guidelines for Americans published under section 5341 of this title.
@ref s 2036a(b) the State agency's permission (src:3151-3152)
`s 2036a(b) the State agency's permission to implement a program` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MAY `s 2036a implement a nutrition education and obesity prevention program`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§§ `(c) Delivery of nutrition education and obesity prevention services`

-- (c)(1) "State agencies may deliver nutrition education and obesity prevention services under a program described in
-- subsection (b) (A) directly to eligible individuals; or (B) through agreements with other State or local agencies or
-- community organizations."
-- src:3154 | (1) In general
-- src:3155 | State agencies may deliver nutrition education and obesity prevention services under a program described in subsection (b)—
-- src:3156 | (A) directly to eligible individuals; or
-- src:3157 | (B) through agreements with other State or local agencies or community organizations.
@ref s 2036a(c)(1) In general (src:3154-3157)
GIVEN delivery IS A `s 2036a delivery`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(1) the State agency may deliver the services this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER delivery
    WHEN `s 2036a directly to eligible individuals` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(A) directly to eligible individuals"
    WHEN `s 2036a through agreements with other State or local agencies or community organizations` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(B) through agreements with other State or local agencies or community organizations"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text does not say "only" or "nothing but"

-- (c)(2)(A) "A State agency that elects to provide nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this subsection
-- shall submit to the Secretary for approval a nutrition education State plan."
-- src:3158 | (2) Nutrition education State plans
-- src:3159 | (A) In general
-- src:3160 | A State agency that elects to provide nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this subsection shall submit to the Secretary for approval a nutrition education State plan.
@ref s 2036a(c)(2)(A) In general (src:3158-3160)
`s 2036a(c)(2)(A) the State agency's duty to submit a nutrition education State plan` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2036a submit a nutrition education State plan to the Secretary for approval`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the State agency that elected to provide services did not submit a nutrition education State plan to the Secretary for approval"

-- src:3158 | (2) Nutrition education State plans
-- src:3159 | (A) In general
-- src:3160 | A State agency that elects to provide nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this subsection shall submit to the Secretary for approval a nutrition education State plan.
@ref s 2036a(c)(2)(A) the duty arises only on election (src:3158-3160)
GIVEN `the State agency elects to provide nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has submitted a nutrition education State plan to the Secretary for approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(2)(A) the State agency has met the duty to submit a plan` MEANS
    IF NOT `the State agency elects to provide nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this subsection`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "a State agency that elects to provide"
    ELSE IF `the State agency has submitted a nutrition education State plan to the Secretary for approval`
         THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall submit to the Secretary for approval a nutrition education State plan"
         ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text sets no time for the plan and says nothing of what follows if it is not yet submitted

-- (c)(2)(B) "A nutrition education State plan shall (i) identify the uses of the funding for local projects; (ii) ensure that the
-- interventions are appropriate for eligible individuals who are members of low-income populations ...; (iii) describe how the State
-- agency shall use an electronic reporting system to ...; and (iv) conform to standards established by the Secretary".
-- src:3161 | (B) Requirements
-- src:3162 | A nutrition education State plan shall—
-- src:3163 | (i) identify the uses of the funding for local projects;
-- src:3164 | (ii) ensure that the interventions are appropriate for eligible individuals who are members of low-income populations by recognizing the constrained resources, and the potential eligibility for Federal food assistance programs, of members of those populations;
-- src:3165 | (iii) describe how the State agency shall use an electronic reporting system to—
-- src:3166 | (I) measure and evaluate the projects; and
-- src:3167 | (II) account for the allowable State agency administrative costs including for—
-- src:3168 | (aa) salaries and benefits of State agency personnel;
-- src:3169 | (bb) office supplies and equipment;
-- src:3170 | (cc) travel costs;
-- src:3171 | (dd) development and production of nutrition education materials;
-- src:3172 | (ee) memberships, subscriptions, and professional activities;
-- src:3173 | (ff) lease or rental costs;
-- src:3174 | (gg) maintenance and repair expenses;
-- src:3175 | (hh) indirect costs; and
-- src:3176 | (ii) cost of using publicly-owned building space; and
-- src:3177 | (iv) conform to standards established by the Secretary through regulations, guidance, or grant award documents.
@ref s 2036a(c)(2)(B) Requirements (src:3161-3177)
GIVEN plan IS A `s 2036a what a plan contains`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(2)(B) the plan contains what it shall` MEANS
    IF plan's `it identifies the uses of the funding for local projects`
       AND plan's `it ensures that the interventions are appropriate for eligible individuals in low-income populations`
       AND plan's `it describes how the State agency shall use an electronic reporting system to measure and evaluate the projects and account for allowable administrative costs`
       AND plan's `it conforms to standards established by the Secretary`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "A nutrition education State plan shall (i) ...; (ii) ...; (iii) ...; and (iv)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the plan shall do and not what follows if it does not

-- (c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) "account for the allowable State agency administrative costs including for (aa) ... (ii)": nine categories.
-- src:3167 | (II) account for the allowable State agency administrative costs including for—
-- src:3168 | (aa) salaries and benefits of State agency personnel;
-- src:3169 | (bb) office supplies and equipment;
-- src:3170 | (cc) travel costs;
-- src:3171 | (dd) development and production of nutrition education materials;
-- src:3172 | (ee) memberships, subscriptions, and professional activities;
-- src:3173 | (ff) lease or rental costs;
-- src:3174 | (gg) maintenance and repair expenses;
-- src:3175 | (hh) indirect costs; and
-- src:3176 | (ii) cost of using publicly-owned building space; and
@ref s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) categories of allowable State agency administrative costs (src:3167-3176)
GIVEN category IS A `s 2036a cost category`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` MEANS
    CONSIDER category
    WHEN `s 2036a some other cost` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "allowable State agency administrative costs including for" does not close the list
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(aa) salaries and benefits of State agency personnel; (bb) office supplies and equipment; (cc) travel costs; (dd) ...; (ii) cost of using publicly-owned building space"

-- (c)(3)(A) "A State agency may use funds provided under this section for any evidence-based allowable use of funds identified by
-- the Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service in consultation with the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and
-- Prevention ..., including (i) ...; (ii) ...; and (iii) ...".
-- src:3179 | (A) In general
-- src:3180 | A State agency may use funds provided under this section for any evidence-based allowable use of funds identified by the Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service of the Department of Agriculture in consultation with the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention of the Department of Health and Human Services, including—
-- src:3181 | (i) individual and group-based nutrition education, health promotion, and intervention strategies;
-- src:3182 | (ii) comprehensive, multilevel interventions at multiple complementary organizational and institutional levels; and
-- src:3183 | (iii) community and public health approaches to improve nutrition.
@ref s 2036a(c)(3)(A) In general (src:3179-3183)
GIVEN `the use is evidence-based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Administrator identified the use as an allowable use of funds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(3)(A) the State agency may use the funds for the use` MEANS
    IF `the use is evidence-based` AND `the Administrator identified the use as an allowable use of funds`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "may use funds provided under this section for any evidence-based allowable use of funds identified by the Administrator"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is for an evidence-based use the Administrator identified

-- src:3181 | (i) individual and group-based nutrition education, health promotion, and intervention strategies;
-- src:3182 | (ii) comprehensive, multilevel interventions at multiple complementary organizational and institutional levels; and
-- src:3183 | (iii) community and public health approaches to improve nutrition.
@ref s 2036a(c)(3)(A)(i) to (iii) the examples (src:3181-3183)
GIVEN use IS A `s 2036a allowable use`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(3)(A) the use is one of the examples the text gives` MEANS
    CONSIDER use
    WHEN `s 2036a some other use` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including" does not close the list
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(i) individual and group-based nutrition education, health promotion, and intervention strategies; (ii) comprehensive, multilevel interventions ...; and (iii) community and public health approaches to improve nutrition"

-- (c)(3)(B) "In identifying allowable uses of funds under subparagraph (A) and in seeking to strengthen delivery, oversight, and
-- evaluation of nutrition education, the Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service shall consult with the Director of the
-- Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, the Director of the National Institute of Food and Agriculture, and outside
-- stakeholders and experts, including (i) ...; (ii) ...; (iii) ...; and (iv) ...".
-- src:3184 | (B) Consultation
-- src:3185 | In identifying allowable uses of funds under subparagraph (A) and in seeking to strengthen delivery, oversight, and evaluation of nutrition education, the Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service shall consult with the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, the Director of the National Institute of Food and Agriculture, and outside stakeholders and experts, including—
-- src:3186 | (i) representatives of the academic and research communities;
-- src:3187 | (ii) nutrition education practitioners;
-- src:3188 | (iii) representatives of State and local governments; and
-- src:3189 | (iv) community organizations that serve low-income populations.
@ref s 2036a(c)(3)(B) Consultation (src:3184-3189)
`s 2036a(c)(3)(B) the Administrator's duty to consult` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2036a consult the Directors and outside stakeholders and experts`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Administrator did not consult the Directors and outside stakeholders and experts"

-- src:3185 | In identifying allowable uses of funds under subparagraph (A) and in seeking to strengthen delivery, oversight, and evaluation of nutrition education, the Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service shall consult with the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, the Director of the National Institute of Food and Agriculture, and outside stakeholders and experts, including—
-- src:3186 | (i) representatives of the academic and research communities;
-- src:3187 | (ii) nutrition education practitioners;
-- src:3188 | (iii) representatives of State and local governments; and
-- src:3189 | (iv) community organizations that serve low-income populations.
@ref s 2036a(c)(3)(B)(i) to (iv) who is consulted (src:3185-3189)
GIVEN stakeholder IS A `s 2036a stakeholder`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(3)(B) the Administrator shall consult this person or body` MEANS
    CONSIDER stakeholder
    WHEN `s 2036a some other person or body` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "outside stakeholders and experts, including" does not close the list
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "consult with the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, the Director of the National Institute of Food and Agriculture, and outside stakeholders and experts, including (i) ... (iv)"

-- (c)(4) "To the maximum extent practicable, State agencies shall notify applicants, participants, and eligible individuals under
-- this chapter of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this section in local communities."
-- src:3190 | (4) Notification
-- src:3191 | To the maximum extent practicable, State agencies shall notify applicants, participants, and eligible individuals under this chapter of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this section in local communities.
@ref s 2036a(c)(4) Notification (src:3190-3191)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant, a participant or an eligible individual under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notifying the person is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(4) the State agency shall notify the person of the availability of the services` MEANS
    IF `the person is an applicant, a participant or an eligible individual under this chapter` AND `notifying the person is practicable`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "To the maximum extent practicable, State agencies shall notify applicants, participants, and eligible individuals"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the maximum extent practicable", and the duty is owed to applicants, participants and eligible individuals

-- src:3190 | (4) Notification
-- src:3191 | To the maximum extent practicable, State agencies shall notify applicants, participants, and eligible individuals under this chapter of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this section in local communities.
@ref s 2036a(c)(4) the State agency's duty (src:3190-3191)
`s 2036a(c)(4) the State agency's duty to notify` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2036a notify applicants, participants and eligible individuals of the availability of services`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the State agency did not notify applicants, participants and eligible individuals of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services"

-- (c)(5) "Subject to the approval of the Secretary, projects carried out with funds received under this section may be
-- coordinated with the expanded food and nutrition education program or other health promotion or nutrition improvement
-- strategies, whether public or privately funded, if the projects carried out with funds received under this section remain under
-- the administrative control of the State agency."
-- src:3192 | (5) Coordination
-- src:3193 | Subject to the approval of the Secretary, projects carried out with funds received under this section may be coordinated with the expanded food and nutrition education program or other health promotion or nutrition improvement strategies, whether public or privately funded, if the projects carried out with funds received under this section remain under the administrative control of the State agency.
@ref s 2036a(c)(5) Coordination (src:3192-3193)
GIVEN `the Secretary has approved the coordination` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the projects remain under the administrative control of the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(5) the projects may be coordinated with other programs and strategies` MEANS
    `s 2036a every one of these holds` (LIST `the approval limb`, `the administrative control limb`)
    WHERE
        `the approval limb` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Secretary has approved the coordination`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Subject to the approval of the Secretary, projects ... may be coordinated"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the approval" is not one of the words that make a failed condition a no
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's approval was not supplied
        `the administrative control limb` MEANS
            IF `the projects remain under the administrative control of the State agency`
            THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "if the projects ... remain under the administrative control of the State agency"
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the projects carried out with funds received under this section remain under the administrative control of the State agency" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

-- (c)(6) "The Secretary shall establish an online clearinghouse that makes available to State agencies, local agencies,
-- institutions of higher education, and community organizations best practices for planning, implementing, and evaluating
-- nutrition education and obesity prevention services".
-- src:3194 | (6) Information clearinghouse
-- src:3195 | The Secretary shall establish an online clearinghouse that makes available to State agencies, local agencies, institutions of higher education, and community organizations best practices for planning, implementing, and evaluating nutrition education and obesity prevention services to ensure that projects carried out with funds received under this section are appropriate for the target population.
@ref s 2036a(c)(6) Information clearinghouse (src:3194-3195)
`s 2036a(c)(6) the Secretary's duty to establish an online clearinghouse` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2036a establish an online clearinghouse`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not establish an online clearinghouse of best practices"

-- (c)(7) "The Secretary shall provide technical assistance to a State agency in developing and implementing a nutrition education
-- State plan, including (A) ...; (B) ...; (C) ...; (D) ...; (E) ...; and (F) ...".
-- src:3196 | (7) Technical assistance
-- src:3197 | The Secretary shall provide technical assistance to a State agency in developing and implementing a nutrition education State plan, including—
-- src:3198 | (A) by identifying common challenges faced by entities described in paragraph (6) that participate in projects carried out with funds received under this section;
-- src:3199 | (B) by coordinating efforts to address those common challenges;
-- src:3200 | (C) by collecting and disseminating information on evidence-based practices relating to nutrition education and obesity prevention;
-- src:3201 | (D) by facilitating communication between and among grantees and subgrantees of funds received under this section;
-- src:3202 | (E) by assisting State agencies in creating or maintaining systems to compile program data; and
-- src:3203 | (F) by performing or assisting with other activities, as determined by the Secretary.
@ref s 2036a(c)(7) Technical assistance (src:3196-3203)
`s 2036a(c)(7) the Secretary's duty to provide technical assistance` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2036a provide technical assistance to the State agency`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not provide technical assistance to the State agency in developing and implementing a nutrition education State plan"

-- src:3198 | (A) by identifying common challenges faced by entities described in paragraph (6) that participate in projects carried out with funds received under this section;
-- src:3199 | (B) by coordinating efforts to address those common challenges;
-- src:3200 | (C) by collecting and disseminating information on evidence-based practices relating to nutrition education and obesity prevention;
-- src:3201 | (D) by facilitating communication between and among grantees and subgrantees of funds received under this section;
-- src:3202 | (E) by assisting State agencies in creating or maintaining systems to compile program data; and
-- src:3203 | (F) by performing or assisting with other activities, as determined by the Secretary.
@ref s 2036a(c)(7)(A) to (F) the forms of help (src:3198-3203)
GIVEN help IS A `s 2036a technical assistance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(7) the help is technical assistance the text lists` MEANS
    CONSIDER help
    WHEN `s 2036a some other help` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "technical assistance ..., including" does not close the list
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(A) by identifying common challenges ...; (B) by coordinating efforts ...; (C) ...; (D) ...; (E) ...; and (F) by performing or assisting with other activities, as determined by the Secretary"

-- (c)(8) "Each State agency that delivers nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this subsection shall submit
-- to the Secretary an annual report, which shall be made publicly available by the Secretary, that includes (A) ...; (B) ...;
-- (C) ...; and (D) ...". The text gives no date for the report.
-- src:3204 | (8) Annual State report
-- src:3205 | Each State agency that delivers nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this subsection shall submit to the Secretary an annual report, which shall be made publicly available by the Secretary, that includes—
-- src:3206 | (A) the use of funds on the State agency’s program, including for each category of allowable State agency administrative costs identified in paragraph (2)(B)(iii)(II);
-- src:3207 | (B) a description of each project carried out by that agency under this subsection, including, with respect to the project, the target population, interventions, educational materials used, key performance indicators used, and evaluations made;
-- src:3208 | (C) a comprehensive analysis of the impacts and outcomes—
-- src:3209 | (i) of the project, including with respect to the elements described in subparagraph (A); and
-- src:3210 | (ii) to the extent practicable, of completed multiyear projects; and
-- src:3211 | (D) the status of any ongoing multiyear project.
@ref s 2036a(c)(8) Annual State report (src:3204-3211)
`s 2036a(c)(8) the State agency's duty to submit an annual report` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2036a submit the annual State report to the Secretary`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the State agency did not submit its annual report to the Secretary"

-- src:3204 | (8) Annual State report
-- src:3205 | Each State agency that delivers nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this subsection shall submit to the Secretary an annual report, which shall be made publicly available by the Secretary, that includes—
-- src:3206 | (A) the use of funds on the State agency’s program, including for each category of allowable State agency administrative costs identified in paragraph (2)(B)(iii)(II);
-- src:3207 | (B) a description of each project carried out by that agency under this subsection, including, with respect to the project, the target population, interventions, educational materials used, key performance indicators used, and evaluations made;
-- src:3208 | (C) a comprehensive analysis of the impacts and outcomes—
-- src:3209 | (i) of the project, including with respect to the elements described in subparagraph (A); and
-- src:3210 | (ii) to the extent practicable, of completed multiyear projects; and
-- src:3211 | (D) the status of any ongoing multiyear project.
@ref s 2036a(c)(8)(A) to (D) what the report includes (src:3204-3211)
GIVEN report IS A `s 2036a state report`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(8) the annual State report includes what it shall` MEANS
    IF report's `the use of funds, including for each category of allowable administrative costs`
       AND report's `a description of each project, with its target population, interventions, educational materials, key performance indicators and evaluations`
       AND report's `a comprehensive analysis of impacts and outcomes of the project and, to the extent practicable, of completed multiyear projects`
       AND report's `the status of any ongoing multiyear project`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "an annual report ... that includes (A) ...; (B) ...; (C) ...; and (D)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the report includes, not what follows if it leaves one out

-- (c)(9) "The Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service, in consultation with the Director of the National Institute of Food
-- and Agriculture, shall annually submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on
-- Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that (A) evaluates the level of coordination between (i) ...; (ii)
-- ...; and (iii) ...; and (B) includes the use of funds on such programs including State agency administrative costs reported by
-- States under paragraph (8)(A)." The text gives no date for the report.
-- src:3212 | (9) Annual Federal report
-- src:3213 | The Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service, in consultation with the Director of the National Institute of Food and Agriculture, shall annually submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that—
-- src:3214 | (A) evaluates the level of coordination between—
-- src:3215 | (i) the nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program under this section;
-- src:3216 | (ii) the expanded food and nutrition education program under section 3175 of this title; and
-- src:3217 | (iii) any other nutrition education program administered by the Department of Agriculture; and
-- src:3218 | (B) includes the use of funds on such programs including State agency administrative costs reported by States under paragraph (8)(A).
@ref s 2036a(c)(9) Annual Federal report (src:3212-3218)
`s 2036a(c)(9) the Administrator's duty to submit an annual report to the Committees` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2036a submit the annual Federal report to the Committees`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Administrator did not submit the annual report to the Committee on Agriculture of the House and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate"

-- src:3212 | (9) Annual Federal report
-- src:3213 | The Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service, in consultation with the Director of the National Institute of Food and Agriculture, shall annually submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that—
-- src:3214 | (A) evaluates the level of coordination between—
-- src:3215 | (i) the nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program under this section;
-- src:3216 | (ii) the expanded food and nutrition education program under section 3175 of this title; and
-- src:3217 | (iii) any other nutrition education program administered by the Department of Agriculture; and
-- src:3218 | (B) includes the use of funds on such programs including State agency administrative costs reported by States under paragraph (8)(A).
@ref s 2036a(c)(9)(A) and (B) what the report evaluates and includes (src:3212-3218)
GIVEN report IS A `s 2036a federal report`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(c)(9) the annual Federal report includes what it shall` MEANS
    IF report's `it evaluates coordination with the expanded food and nutrition education program`
       AND report's `it evaluates coordination with any other nutrition education program administered by the Department of Agriculture`
       AND report's `it evaluates coordination of the nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program itself`
       AND report's `it includes the use of funds on such programs, including State agency administrative costs reported under paragraph (8)(A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "a report that (A) evaluates the level of coordination between (i) ...; (ii) ...; and (iii) ...; and (B) includes the use of funds"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the report does, not what follows if it leaves one out

§§ `(d) Funding`

-- (d)(1) "Of funds made available each fiscal year under section 2027(a)(1) of this title, the Secretary shall reserve for
-- allocation to State agencies to carry out the nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program under this section, to
-- remain available for obligation for a period of 2 fiscal years (A) for fiscal year 2011, $375,000,000; (B) for fiscal year 2012,
-- $388,000,000; (C) for fiscal year 2013, $285,000,000; (D) for fiscal year 2014, $401,000,000; (E) for fiscal year 2015,
-- $407,000,000; and (F) for each of fiscal years 2016 through 2025, the applicable amount during the preceding fiscal year, as
-- adjusted to reflect any increases for the 12-month period ending the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban
-- Consumers". The increases are published figures, so they are a conditional input: one percent per fiscal year from 2016, in order.
-- Only increases count ("any increases"): a decrease leaves the amount unchanged (fork FR-36a-1).
-- src:3220 | (1) In general
-- src:3221 | Of funds made available each fiscal year under section 2027(a)(1) of this title, the Secretary shall reserve for allocation to State agencies to carry out the nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program under this section, to remain available for obligation for a period of 2 fiscal years—
-- src:3222 | (A) for fiscal year 2011, $375,000,000;
-- src:3223 | (B) for fiscal year 2012, $388,000,000;
-- src:3224 | (C) for fiscal year 2013, $285,000,000;
-- src:3225 | (D) for fiscal year 2014, $401,000,000;
-- src:3226 | (E) for fiscal year 2015, $407,000,000; and
-- src:3227 | (F) for each of fiscal years 2016 through 2025, the applicable amount during the preceding fiscal year, as adjusted to reflect any increases for the 12-month period ending the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor.
@ref s 2036a(d)(1) In general (src:3220-3227)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the percent increase in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers for the 12-month period ending each preceding June 30, for fiscal years 2016 on, in order` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2036a(d)(1) the amount reserved for the fiscal year, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2011 THEN JUST 375000000   -- (A) "for fiscal year 2011, $375,000,000"
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2012 THEN JUST 388000000   -- (B) "for fiscal year 2012, $388,000,000"
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2013 THEN JUST 285000000   -- (C) "for fiscal year 2013, $285,000,000"
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2014 THEN JUST 401000000   -- (D) "for fiscal year 2014, $401,000,000"
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2015 THEN JUST 407000000   -- (E) "for fiscal year 2015, $407,000,000"
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2016 AND `fiscal year` AT MOST 2025
           THEN IF count `the percent increase in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers for the 12-month period ending each preceding June 30, for fiscal years 2016 on, in order` LESS THAN `fiscal year` MINUS 2015
                THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Consumer Price Index figure for that year was not supplied
                ELSE CONSIDER `s 2036a(d)(1) the amount reserved for the fiscal year, in dollars` (`fiscal year` MINUS 1) `the percent increase in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers for the 12-month period ending each preceding June 30, for fiscal years 2016 on, in order`
                     WHEN JUST previous THEN JUST (previous TIMES (1 PLUS (IF at `the percent increase in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers for the 12-month period ending each preceding June 30, for fiscal years 2016 on, in order` (`fiscal year` MINUS 2016) AT LEAST 0 THEN at `the percent increase in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers for the 12-month period ending each preceding June 30, for fiscal years 2016 on, in order` (`fiscal year` MINUS 2016) ELSE 0) DIVIDED BY 100))   -- (F) "the applicable amount during the preceding fiscal year, as adjusted to reflect any increases"
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an earlier year's figure was not supplied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names fiscal years 2011 through 2025

-- src:3220 | (1) In general
-- src:3221 | Of funds made available each fiscal year under section 2027(a)(1) of this title, the Secretary shall reserve for allocation to State agencies to carry out the nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program under this section, to remain available for obligation for a period of 2 fiscal years—
@ref s 2036a(d)(1) the Secretary's duty to reserve (src:3220-3221)
`s 2036a(d)(1) the Secretary's duty to reserve the funds for allocation to State agencies` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2036a reserve the funds for allocation to State agencies`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not reserve the funds for allocation to State agencies"

-- (d)(2)(A) "Of the funds set aside under paragraph (1), as determined by the Secretary (i) for each of fiscal years 2011 through
-- 2013, 100 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in direct proportion to the amount of funding that the State received for
-- carrying out section 2020(f) ... during fiscal year 2009, as reported to the Secretary as of February 2010; and (ii) subject to
-- a reallocation under subparagraph (B) (I) for fiscal year 2014 (aa) 90 percent ... in accordance with clause (i); and (bb) 10
-- percent ... based on the respective share of each State of the number of individuals participating in the supplemental nutrition
-- assistance program during the 12-month period ending the preceding January 31; (II) 2015: 80 and 20; (III) 2016: 70 and 30;
-- (IV) 2017: 60 and 40; (V) fiscal year 2018 and each fiscal year thereafter: 50 and 50."
-- src:3229 | (A) Initial allocation
-- src:3230 | Of the funds set aside under paragraph (1), as determined by the Secretary—
-- src:3231 | (i) for each of fiscal years 2011 through 2013, 100 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in direct proportion to the amount of funding that the State received for carrying out section 2020(f) of this title (as that section existed on the day before the December 13, 2010) during fiscal year 2009, as reported to the Secretary as of February 2010; and
-- src:3232 | (ii) subject to a reallocation under subparagraph (B)—
-- src:3233 | (I) for fiscal year 2014—
-- src:3234 | (aa) 90 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3235 | (bb) 10 percent shall be allocated to State agencies based on the respective share of each State of the number of individuals participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program during the 12-month period ending the preceding January 31;
-- src:3236 | (II) for fiscal year 2015—
-- src:3237 | (aa) 80 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3238 | (bb) 20 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb);
-- src:3239 | (III) for fiscal year 2016—
-- src:3240 | (aa) 70 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3241 | (bb) 30 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb);
-- src:3242 | (IV) for fiscal year 2017—
-- src:3243 | (aa) 60 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3244 | (bb) 40 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb); and
-- src:3245 | (V) for fiscal year 2018 and each fiscal year thereafter—
-- src:3246 | (aa) 50 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3247 | (bb) 50 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb).
@ref s 2036a(d)(2)(A) Initial allocation (the two percentages) (src:3229-3247)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2036a(d)(2)(A) the percent allocated in proportion to fiscal year 2009 funding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2011 AND `fiscal year` AT MOST 2013 THEN JUST 100   -- (i) "for each of fiscal years 2011 through 2013, 100 percent"
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2014 THEN JUST 90   -- (ii)(I)(aa)
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2015 THEN JUST 80   -- (ii)(II)(aa)
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2016 THEN JUST 70   -- (ii)(III)(aa)
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2017 THEN JUST 60   -- (ii)(IV)(aa)
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2018 THEN JUST 50   -- (ii)(V)(aa)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no allocation is set for fiscal year 2010 or before

-- src:3229 | (A) Initial allocation
-- src:3230 | Of the funds set aside under paragraph (1), as determined by the Secretary—
-- src:3231 | (i) for each of fiscal years 2011 through 2013, 100 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in direct proportion to the amount of funding that the State received for carrying out section 2020(f) of this title (as that section existed on the day before the December 13, 2010) during fiscal year 2009, as reported to the Secretary as of February 2010; and
-- src:3232 | (ii) subject to a reallocation under subparagraph (B)—
-- src:3233 | (I) for fiscal year 2014—
-- src:3234 | (aa) 90 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3235 | (bb) 10 percent shall be allocated to State agencies based on the respective share of each State of the number of individuals participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program during the 12-month period ending the preceding January 31;
-- src:3236 | (II) for fiscal year 2015—
-- src:3237 | (aa) 80 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3238 | (bb) 20 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb);
-- src:3239 | (III) for fiscal year 2016—
-- src:3240 | (aa) 70 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3241 | (bb) 30 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb);
-- src:3242 | (IV) for fiscal year 2017—
-- src:3243 | (aa) 60 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3244 | (bb) 40 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb); and
-- src:3245 | (V) for fiscal year 2018 and each fiscal year thereafter—
-- src:3246 | (aa) 50 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3247 | (bb) 50 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb).
@ref s 2036a(d)(2)(A) Initial allocation (the participation percentage) (src:3229-3247)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2036a(d)(2)(A) the percent allocated in proportion to participation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2011 AND `fiscal year` AT MOST 2013 THEN JUST 0   -- (i) allocates 100 percent by fiscal year 2009 funding, which leaves none
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2014 THEN JUST 10   -- (ii)(I)(bb)
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2015 THEN JUST 20   -- (ii)(II)(bb)
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2016 THEN JUST 30   -- (ii)(III)(bb)
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2017 THEN JUST 40   -- (ii)(IV)(bb)
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2018 THEN JUST 50   -- (ii)(V)(bb)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no allocation is set for fiscal year 2010 or before

-- A State agency's share of the funds set aside, before any reallocation under (B): the two shares are fractions of 1.
-- src:3229 | (A) Initial allocation
-- src:3230 | Of the funds set aside under paragraph (1), as determined by the Secretary—
-- src:3231 | (i) for each of fiscal years 2011 through 2013, 100 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in direct proportion to the amount of funding that the State received for carrying out section 2020(f) of this title (as that section existed on the day before the December 13, 2010) during fiscal year 2009, as reported to the Secretary as of February 2010; and
-- src:3232 | (ii) subject to a reallocation under subparagraph (B)—
-- src:3233 | (I) for fiscal year 2014—
-- src:3234 | (aa) 90 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3235 | (bb) 10 percent shall be allocated to State agencies based on the respective share of each State of the number of individuals participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program during the 12-month period ending the preceding January 31;
-- src:3236 | (II) for fiscal year 2015—
-- src:3237 | (aa) 80 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3238 | (bb) 20 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb);
-- src:3239 | (III) for fiscal year 2016—
-- src:3240 | (aa) 70 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3241 | (bb) 30 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb);
-- src:3242 | (IV) for fiscal year 2017—
-- src:3243 | (aa) 60 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3244 | (bb) 40 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb); and
-- src:3245 | (V) for fiscal year 2018 and each fiscal year thereafter—
-- src:3246 | (aa) 50 percent shall be allocated to State agencies in accordance with clause (i); and
-- src:3247 | (bb) 50 percent shall be allocated in accordance with subclause (I)(bb).
@ref s 2036a(d)(2)(A) Initial allocation (a State agency's share) (src:3229-3247)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the funds set aside for the fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the State agency's share of the amount of funding all State agencies received for carrying out section 2020(f) during fiscal year 2009, as reported as of February 2010` IS A NUMBER
      `the State's share of the number of individuals participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program during the 12-month period ending the preceding January 31` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2036a(d)(2)(A) the State agency's allocation before any reallocation, in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2036a(d)(2)(A) the percent allocated in proportion to fiscal year 2009 funding` `fiscal year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no allocation is set for that fiscal year
    WHEN JUST byFunding THEN
        CONSIDER `s 2036a(d)(2)(A) the percent allocated in proportion to participation` `fiscal year`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no allocation is set for that fiscal year
        WHEN JUST byParticipation THEN JUST (`the funds set aside for the fiscal year, in dollars` TIMES (byFunding TIMES `the State agency's share of the amount of funding all State agencies received for carrying out section 2020(f) during fiscal year 2009, as reported as of February 2010` PLUS byParticipation TIMES `the State's share of the number of individuals participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program during the 12-month period ending the preceding January 31`) DIVIDED BY 100)

-- (d)(2)(B)(i) "If the Secretary determines that a State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated ... or in the case of a
-- State agency that elects not to receive the entire amount of funds allocated, the Secretary shall reallocate the unexpended
-- funds to other States ... that have approved State plans under which the State agencies may expend the reallocated funds."
-- src:3248 | (B) Reallocation
-- src:3249 | (i) In general
-- src:3250 | If the Secretary determines that a State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated to the State agency for a fiscal year under paragraph (1) or in the case of a State agency that elects not to receive the entire amount of funds allocated to the State agency for a fiscal year, the Secretary shall reallocate the unexpended funds to other States during the fiscal year or the subsequent fiscal year (as determined by the Secretary) that have approved State plans under which the State agencies may expend the reallocated funds.
@ref s 2036a(d)(2)(B)(i) Reallocation (src:3248-3250)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines that the State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State agency elects not to receive the entire amount of funds allocated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other State has an approved State plan under which its State agency may expend the reallocated funds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(d)(2)(B)(i) the Secretary shall reallocate the unexpended funds to the other State` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the trigger`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Secretary determines that a State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated ... or in the case of a State agency that elects not to receive" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the other State has an approved State plan under which its State agency may expend the reallocated funds`
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the Secretary shall reallocate the unexpended funds to other States ... that have approved State plans"
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reallocation is to States that have approved State plans
    WHERE
        `the trigger` MEANS
            `s 2036a at least one of these holds` (LIST `the Secretary determines that the State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated`, JUST `the State agency elects not to receive the entire amount of funds allocated`)

-- src:3248 | (B) Reallocation
-- src:3249 | (i) In general
-- src:3250 | If the Secretary determines that a State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated to the State agency for a fiscal year under paragraph (1) or in the case of a State agency that elects not to receive the entire amount of funds allocated to the State agency for a fiscal year, the Secretary shall reallocate the unexpended funds to other States during the fiscal year or the subsequent fiscal year (as determined by the Secretary) that have approved State plans under which the State agencies may expend the reallocated funds.
@ref s 2036a(d)(2)(B)(i) the Secretary's duty (src:3248-3250)
`s 2036a(d)(2)(B)(i) the Secretary's duty to reallocate` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2036a reallocate the unexpended funds to other States`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not reallocate the unexpended funds to other States"

-- (d)(2)(B)(ii) "(I) Any reallocated funds received by a State agency under clause (i) for a fiscal year shall be considered to
-- be part of the fiscal year 2009 base allocation ... for purposes of determining allocation under subparagraph (A) for the
-- subsequent fiscal year. (II) Any funds surrendered by a State agency under clause (i) shall not be considered to be part of the
-- fiscal year 2009 base allocation".
-- src:3251 | (ii) Effect of additional funds
-- src:3252 | (I) Funds received
-- src:3253 | Any reallocated funds received by a State agency under clause (i) for a fiscal year shall be considered to be part of the fiscal year 2009 base allocation of funds to the State agency for that fiscal year for purposes of determining allocation under subparagraph (A) for the subsequent fiscal year.
-- src:3254 | (II) Funds surrendered
-- src:3255 | Any funds surrendered by a State agency under clause (i) shall not be considered to be part of the fiscal year 2009 base allocation of funds to a State agency for that fiscal year for purposes of determining allocation under subparagraph (A) for the subsequent fiscal year.
@ref s 2036a(d)(2)(B)(ii) Effect of additional funds (src:3251-3255)
GIVEN `how the funds came to the State agency` IS A `s 2036a how funds came to the State agency`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(d)(2)(B)(ii) the funds are part of the State agency's fiscal year 2009 base allocation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the funds came to the State agency`
    WHEN `s 2036a received through a reallocation` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Any reallocated funds received by a State agency under clause (i) ... shall be considered to be part of the fiscal year 2009 base allocation"
    WHEN `s 2036a surrendered by the State agency` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any funds surrendered by a State agency under clause (i) shall not be considered to be part of the fiscal year 2009 base allocation"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (ii) speaks of funds received through a reallocation and funds surrendered

-- (d)(3)(A) "Grants awarded under this section shall be the only source of Federal financial participation under this chapter in
-- nutrition education and obesity prevention."
-- src:3256 | (3) Limitation on Federal financial participation
-- src:3257 | (A) In general
-- src:3258 | Grants awarded under this section shall be the only source of Federal financial participation under this chapter in nutrition education and obesity prevention.
@ref s 2036a(d)(3)(A) In general (src:3256-3258)
GIVEN source IS A `s 2036a source of Federal financial participation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(d)(3)(A) the source is a source of Federal financial participation in nutrition education and obesity prevention` MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `s 2036a a grant awarded under this section` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Grants awarded under this section shall be the only source of Federal financial participation under this chapter in nutrition education and obesity prevention"
    WHEN `s 2036a any other source` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be the only source of Federal financial participation"

-- (d)(3)(B) "Any costs of nutrition education and obesity prevention in excess of the grants authorized under this section shall
-- not be eligible for reimbursement under section 2025(a) of this title."
-- src:3259 | (B) Exclusion
-- src:3260 | Any costs of nutrition education and obesity prevention in excess of the grants authorized under this section shall not be eligible for reimbursement under section 2025(a) of this title.
@ref s 2036a(d)(3)(B) Exclusion (src:3259-3260)
GIVEN `the cost of nutrition education and obesity prevention, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the grants authorized under this section, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(d)(3)(B) the cost is eligible for reimbursement under section 2025(a)` MEANS
    IF `the cost of nutrition education and obesity prevention, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the grants authorized under this section, in dollars`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any costs of nutrition education and obesity prevention in excess of the grants authorized under this section shall not be eligible for reimbursement under section 2025(a)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (B) speaks only of costs in excess of the grants; reimbursement of the rest is for section 2025(a)

§§ `(e) Implementation`

-- (e) "Not later than January 1, 2012, the Secretary shall publish in the Federal Register a description of the requirements for
-- the receipt of a grant under this section." The deadline is a calendar date, so this is a function over dates.
-- src:3261 | (e) Implementation
-- src:3262 | Not later than January 1, 2012, the Secretary shall publish in the Federal Register a description of the requirements for the receipt of a grant under this section.
@ref s 2036a(e) Implementation (src:3261-3262)
GIVEN `the date the Secretary published the description` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036a(e) the Secretary published the description in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the Secretary published the description`
    WHEN JUST published THEN
        IF published AT MOST (Date 1 1 2012)
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Not later than January 1, 2012" is met
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than January 1, 2012, the Secretary shall publish"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF today GREATER THAN (Date 1 1 2012)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than January 1, 2012, the Secretary shall publish" (the date has passed and nothing was published)
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date has not yet passed
